# nr-office-ooxml-xlsx-shift-pivot: integration fragment

Two modules of the crate mixdog-ooxml: `xlsx_reference_shift` (portable-xlsx-reference-shift.mjs: reference rewriting when
rows or columns are inserted or deleted, sheets renamed, deleted or copied, sorted formulas, the calculation chain) and
`pivot` (portable-pivot.mjs: pivot field summary, cache definition and records, table part, the computed grid). No protocol
method, service or SERVICE_PENDING name belongs to them.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-ooxml/src/lib.rs

After `pub mod xlsx_cell_values;` add:

    pub mod xlsx_reference_shift;
    pub mod pivot;

## native/core/crates/mixdog-ooxml/Cargo.toml

New dependency edge between workspace crates. In [dependencies], after `mixdog-ooxml-text = { workspace = true }`, add:

    mixdog-xlsx-formula = { workspace = true }

(`mixdog-xlsx-formula` is already a workspace member and a [workspace.dependencies] entry; it depends on mixdog-js and
mixdog-office-base only, so the edge makes no cycle.)

## native/core/Cargo.lock

In the `[[package]]` entry `mixdog-ooxml`, add `"mixdog-xlsx-formula",` to its `dependencies` list (keep the list sorted: it
goes after `"mixdog-workspace-hack",`). No other entry changes; every crate the two modules use (mixdog-js, serde_json) is
already a dependency of mixdog-ooxml.

## native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json

In the "sets" list (kept sorted by set name), after the entry of "office-sheet-xml" and before "office-startup", add:

    {
      "command": "node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-shift-pivot.mjs --tree <tree>",
      "fileCount": 1,
      "manifest": "office-shift-pivot/MANIFEST.json",
      "manifestSha256": "ea97b1ebc7d9cb99c0fef7ab2f34bc8acf3df9e1146dbab38c812a11fed1690b",
      "recorder": "benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-shift-pivot.mjs",
      "set": "office-shift-pivot",
      "totalBytes": 642586
    }

(Recompute manifestSha256 and totalBytes from the committed office-shift-pivot/MANIFEST.json and golden.json if the tool that
keeps this file reorders or reformats them. The recorder imports benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/lib/common.mjs, which is the
integration tree's own; it was run against the product tree with `--tree C:/Project/mixdog`.)

## Not compiled

The two modules, their unit tests and tests/twin_shift_pivot.rs were written without cargo (the wave is compiled by the lead);
rustfmt parsed both source files. The first build of mixdog-ooxml with the lib.rs and Cargo.toml lines above, and
`cargo test -p mixdog-ooxml`, is the check. tests/twin_shift_pivot.rs replays native/core/fixtures/office-shift-pivot and needs
no Node; twin_live_shift_pivot (ignored) re-records through Node.

## For the later tasks that call these modules

Node's callers (portable-xlsx-operations.mjs, portable-xlsx-range-layout.mjs, portable-xlsx-pivot-ops.mjs) use these
signatures: `shift_worksheet_cells(zip, sheets, sheet, xml, ShiftRequest { rows, from, amount, insert, op })`,
`rename_sheet_references(zip, sheets, sheet, to: Option<&str>, op)` (None is a deleted sheet), `copied_sheet_xml`,
`copy_sheet_parts`, `drop_calculation_chain`, `sorted_formula(formula, row_delta)`, `inherited_rows(xml, from, amount)`,
`summarize_pivot_fields(headers, records, axes)` and `write_pivot_table(zip, &PivotRequest { layout, records, .. })`.
Errors are the Node message text (`Portable insert_rows at Data row 6 cannot rewrite ... Office backend ...`) as a String.
